# Call-site ledger of fastjsonschema at 9d3f5ee74d0749ef4abf695f370437aca5f9d56c (v2.22.3).
# Decide every `undecided` line; see macro-benchmark/README.md.
#
# fastjsonschema.md has the judgements. In short:
# - CodeGenerator.l is decorated with @indent (generator.py:250): every
#   self.l(...) calls fastjsonschema.indent.indent.wrapper, which calls l back
#   (indent.py:10) and returns an Indent; `with self.l(...)` therefore runs
#   Indent.__enter__ and Indent.__exit__.
# - The generated validation code that compile() runs with exec has no node
#   (README scope ruling 4; micro-benchmark "Nodes"). The call in its module
#   code, type(None), belongs to compile (micro-benchmark "Scopes without a
#   node"); the package classes that the generated functions instantiate
#   (JsonSchemaValueException, JsonSchemaValuesException) are callbacks of the
#   package site that calls a generated function (validate, __init__.py:172).
# - Schemas are JSON values: `definition` is annotated dict[str, Any] | bool
#   (B4), and its sub-schemas are dicts (JSON objects), lists, strs, numbers,
#   bools and None, as the documentation's examples and json.loads give them.
# - The code generators that the package makes are CodeGeneratorDraft04, 06,
#   07 and 2019 (_get_code_generator_class); the tests also make a
#   CodeGeneratorDraft07 without a resolver (tests/conftest.py:25).
default reject fastjsonschema.generator.CodeGenerator.l: CodeGenerator.l is decorated with @indent (generator.py:250), so the class attribute l is the function wrapper that indent returns; every self.l(...) calls fastjsonschema.indent.indent.wrapper, and only wrapper calls the original l back, through its parameter func (indent.py:10)

